                                                "sense_id": "758ab3ed-ff47-397b-86a8-7ed4fd24c9de",
                                                "text": "http://undergroundcoal.com.au/fundamentals/01_process.aspx\nOnce access has been gained into the coal seam, workings are developed by mining a series of roadways (or headings). These roadways are tunnels largely, if not totally, within the seam, usually rectangular in shape though on occasions they may have an arched or even circular profile."
